      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Extension",
      "body": "Keep stacking 3rds past the 7th and you reach the 9th, the 11th and the 13th. Notes past the 7th are called **extensions**: they extend a 7th chord.\n\n**Why it matters:** Jazz and gospel players add extensions for colour. A chart that says C9 or G13 is asking for them.",
